# exodusii Agent Guide

exodusii owns reading, writing, querying, comparing, and summarizing Exodus II finite-element databases for this repository.

## Task Routing

- If you are unfamiliar with exodusii, start with `exodusii-agent-orientation`.
- If you are extracting variables or producing JSON from a database, start with `exodusii-querying`.
- If you are writing Python code against exodusii, start with `exodusii-python-api`.
- If you are comparing a result against a baseline, start with `exodusii-comparison`.
- If you are selecting entities inside a shape or computing lineouts, start with `exodusii-geometry`.
- If you are computing statistics or mass inside a region, start with `exodusii-region-reduce`.
- If you are working with decomposed `FILE.exo.N.n` pieces, start with `exodusii-parallel-files`.
- If you are writing a new database, start with `exodusii-writing`.

## Installed Skills

@@SKILL_MAP@@

## Suggested Command Palette

- `python -m exodusii learn capabilities overview`
- `python -m exodusii learn capabilities commands`
- `python -m exodusii learn skills list`
- `python -m exodusii inspect FILE.exo`
- `python -m exodusii variables FILE.exo`
- `python -m exodusii query FILE.exo --select n/TEMP --time last`
- `python -m exodusii stats FILE.exo --select e/ENERGY --time last --by-block`
- `python -m exodusii diff GOLD.exo TEST.exo`

## Database-First Guidance

- Use `inspect`, `variables`, `blocks`, `sets`, and `times` before guessing names or indices.
- Use the JSON commands and the modern Python API before reading the NetCDF file directly.

Generated by `python -m exodusii agent bootstrap`.
